cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use research-timeline in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "research-timeline: track, validate, and export the research process as a typed JSON timeline"
abstract: >-
  research-timeline documents the process of research, not just its artifacts:
  every milestone of a project (the first AI interaction that shaped the
  protocol, QPU commits with their evidence, pivots, controls, submissions,
  publications) is recorded in a single versioned JSON file with typed events,
  quantitative metrics, and supporting evidence. The timeline validates against
  a JSON Schema (draft-07), diffs cleanly with git, passes CI, and exports to
  LaTeX tables, Markdown, standalone HTML, schema.org JSON-LD, CSV, and a
  publication-ready Gantt chart (TikZ).
